<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34083" root="فضل" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِضْلَةٌ</span></b>  is a n. of the same kind as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جِلْسَةٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِكْبَةٌ</span>: (AZ, S, O, TA:) one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهُ لَحَسَنُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفِضْلَةِ</span>, meaning [<i>Verily he is comely in respect of</i>]
<i>the manner of wearing a single garment.</i> (S, * O, *
K, * TA.)

